The TLS stack has no wasm32 target.

`ureq` + `rustls` are pinned to the `ring` provider, and `ring` builds its
assembly and C through a build script with no wasm32-wasip2 path — so the
cross-build fails in the dependency, before reaching any of this package's own
code.

A browser program does not want this crate anyway: `--html` reaches the network
through the host, not through a native TLS stack.  What is missing is the
headless wasip2 target, and that needs a wasm-capable TLS provider rather than a
change here.

Delete this file when `rustls` can be built for wasm32 here — most likely by
moving off the `ring` provider — and the gate will hold the package to it.
